# ZeGFX Full Subsystem Audit — Honest Status Report

> [!CAUTION]
> This audit uses three honest tiers. **"Wired"** means Godot's rendering loop literally calls a bridge method. But **"wired" does NOT mean "doing GPU work"** — most bridge methods log a message and `return true`. This distinction matters.

---

## Classification Legend

| Symbol | Meaning |
|:---:|:---|
| 🟢 | **WIRED & EXECUTING** — Godot calls it AND it does real work (math, COM queries, GPU dispatch) |
| 🟡 | **WIRED BUT HOLLOW** — Godot calls bridge method, but method body is `print_verbose(); return true;` — no GPU work |
| 🔴 | **COMPLETELY UNWIRED** — No bridge method, no Godot callsite, ZeGFX code exists but is never invoked |

